{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/604070-claiming-trophies-from-beasts","id":604070,"title":"Claiming Trophies from Beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-26T13:49:14-07:00","id":604070,"title":"Claiming Trophies from Beasts","content":"In the original preview there was a reference to Heroes taking trophies from their kills in the short section on Hercules, and in both versions of the Rampant Inheritance mention is made of collecting blood to sell. What I'm wondering about is, how does one remove pieces of a Horror from the Lair? Is it as simple as taking a tooth or claw or fang and returning to the real world? Normally the Horror cannot completely leave the Lair except through Inheritance, so I'm not sure how parts of it could, unless being separated from the Horror those parts are &quot;dead&quot; and thus able to separate from the Lair. I'm not sure how that interpretation works with and Unfettered Inheritance though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T15:23:15-07:00","id":604228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/604070-claiming-trophies-from-beasts#post604070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the original preview there was a reference to Heroes taking trophies from their kills in the short section on Hercules, and in both versions of the Rampant Inheritance mention is made of collecting blood to sell. What I'm wondering about is, how does one remove pieces of a Horror from the Lair? Is it as simple as taking a tooth or claw or fang and returning to the real world? Normally the Horror cannot completely leave the Lair except through Inheritance, so I'm not sure how parts of it could, unless being separated from the Horror those parts are &quot;dead&quot; and thus able to separate from the Lair. I'm not sure how that interpretation works with and Unfettered Inheritance though.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could portray that as a special Anathema for particularly ballsy Heroes to use. I doubt many other ways of killing a Beast would be as satisfying for Heroes as using the Beast's weapons against it. I'm getting God Of War flashbacks already.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}